      ":question/problem": "Express the following as a constant multiple of a single trigonometric ratio.\n\n$$\n-3\\sin\\left(\\frac{2\\pi}{11}\\right)\\cos\\left(\\frac{2\\pi}{11}\\right)\n$$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Put $x=\\frac{2\\pi}{11}$. Recall $2\\sin x\\cos x=\\sin(2x)$.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-3\\sin x\\cos x &=-\\frac{3}{2}\\left[2\\sin x\\cos x\\right] \\\\ &=-\\frac{3}{2}\\sin(2x)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstitute $x=\\frac{2\\pi}{11}$ and double the whole angle: $2x=\\frac{4\\pi}{11}$. The result is\n\n$$\n-\\frac{3}{2}\\sin\\left(\\frac{4\\pi}{11}\\right) .\n$$",
